# ============================================================================
# NODE.JS TUTORIAL PROJECT - COMPREHENSIVE .GITIGNORE
# ============================================================================
# 
# Comprehensive Git ignore file for Node.js tutorial project demonstrating
# progressive web application development from basic HTTP server implementation
# to production-ready deployment with PM2 cluster mode, comprehensive testing,
# and cross-platform Flask migration comparison.
#
# Supports:
# - Node.js v22.x LTS with Express.js v5.1.0
# - PM2 v6.0.8 cluster mode deployment  
# - Jest/Mocha testing frameworks with comprehensive coverage
# - Helmet.js security implementation with SSL certificate management
# - Flask cross-platform migration and feature parity validation
# - Modern development tooling (ESLint, Prettier, TypeScript)
# - Production deployment with zero-downtime capabilities
#
# Security Features:
# - Excludes sensitive environment files while preserving templates
# - Protects SSL certificates and private cryptographic material
# - Excludes security scan results that may contain sensitive information
# - Maintains directory structure through strategic .gitkeep preservation
#
# ============================================================================

# Node.js Dependencies and Package Managers
# Excludes all package manager artifacts while preserving package.json definitions
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Environment Configuration
# Excludes sensitive environment files while preserving documentation templates
.env
.env.local
.env.development
.env.test
.env.production
!.env.example
!.env.template

# Logs and Monitoring
# Excludes runtime log files while preserving directory structure for PM2
logs/*.log
logs/**/*.log
logs/**/*.gz
*.log
pm2.log
combined.log
access.log
error.log
out.log
!logs/.gitkeep

# Test Coverage and Reports
# Excludes generated coverage reports while maintaining testing infrastructure
coverage/
*.lcov
.nyc_output/
junit.xml
test-results.xml
coverage-final.json
!coverage/.gitkeep
!coverage/jest/.gitkeep
!coverage/mocha/.gitkeep
!coverage/c8/.gitkeep

# Build Artifacts and Temporary Files
# Excludes all build outputs and temporary processing files
dist/
build/
public/build/
tmp/
temp/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
*.tgz
*.tar.gz

# SSL Certificates and Private Keys
# Excludes cryptographic material while preserving certificate infrastructure
certificates/*.crt
certificates/*.key
certificates/*.pem
certificates/*.p12
certificates/*.pfx
*.crt
*.key
*.pem
!certificates/.gitkeep
!certificates/README.md

# PM2 Runtime and Process Files
# Excludes PM2 runtime artifacts while preserving ecosystem configuration
.pm2/
pm2.json
ecosystem.json
pids/
dumps/
pm2-dev.json

# Python Flask Cross-Platform Support
# Excludes Python artifacts for cross-platform development compatibility
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
env/
venv/
.venv/
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# Development Tools and IDE
# Excludes IDE-specific settings and development tool cache files
.vscode/settings.json
.vscode/launch.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache
.prettier-cache/

# Operating System Files
# Excludes platform-specific system files for cross-platform compatibility
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# Security Scanning and Reports
# Excludes security assessment files that may contain sensitive information
*.sarif
.snyk
security-report.json
vulnerability-scan.json
audit-results.json

# Performance Testing Results
# Excludes performance benchmarking outputs and load testing results
benchmark-results/
load-test-results/
artillery-report.json
autocannon-results.json
performance-metrics.json

# Docker and Container Files (if used)
# Excludes container-specific files while preserving base configuration
.dockerignore
docker-compose.override.yml

# Backup and Archive Files
# Excludes backup files and temporary archives created during development
*.backup
*.bak
*.old
*.orig
*.rej

# Miscellaneous
# Additional Node.js and JavaScript ecosystem exclusions
.npm
.node_repl_history
*.seed
*.pid.lock
jspm_packages/
web_modules/
lerna-debug.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# ============================================================================
# EDUCATIONAL NOTES AND BEST PRACTICES
# ============================================================================
#
# This .gitignore demonstrates professional version control practices including:
#
# 1. SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS:
#    - Environment files (.env*) excluded to protect sensitive configuration
#    - SSL certificates excluded to prevent accidental key exposure
#    - Security scan results excluded to avoid information disclosure
#
# 2. PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATIONS:
#    - Node modules excluded to prevent repository bloat (>100MB saved)
#    - Log files excluded to maintain repository performance
#    - Build artifacts excluded as they're regenerated from source
#
# 3. CROSS-PLATFORM COMPATIBILITY:
#    - Python files excluded for Flask migration support
#    - OS-specific files excluded for multi-platform development
#    - IDE settings excluded to support diverse development environments
#
# 4. PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT:
#    - PM2 runtime files excluded while preserving configuration
#    - Certificate directory maintained for SSL infrastructure
#    - Log directory preserved for production logging pipeline
#
# 5. TESTING INFRASTRUCTURE:
#    - Coverage directories maintained via .gitkeep files
#    - Test artifacts excluded while preserving test configuration
#    - Performance test results excluded but infrastructure maintained
#
# 6. DEVELOPMENT WORKFLOW:
#    - Package manager lock files excluded for flexibility
#    - Development cache excluded for consistent builds
#    - Temporary files excluded to maintain clean workspace
#
# MAINTENANCE RECOMMENDATIONS:
# - Review and update patterns quarterly for new tools
# - Test effectiveness with `git status` and `git check-ignore`
# - Validate directory preservation through .gitkeep files
# - Monitor repository size and performance impact
#
# ============================================================================